# DTF tier manifest: pypi-age-gate-substitute-scanned  (artifact-keeper#5075, PR #5077)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + the canned PyPI upstream of the
# pypi-age-gate-pep440-lookup tier (mock-pypi, profile upstreams.mockpypi-agegate)
# serving `cuda-toolkit` with Warehouse JSON publish times: 13.4.2 (old) and
# 13.5.0 (uploaded a day ago). Scanning uses the backend image's bundled Grype
# and seeded DB (no network).
#
# WHAT IT PROVES (#5075): when the download age gate withholds a young version,
# a PyPI Remote answers with the newest older version it holds (the
# last-known-good substitute). On a Remote that scans on proxy, that substitute
# download goes through the same scan-on-proxy route as any other distribution
# download (#5077), so it carries the scan result header like any other
# distribution download and records a digest-keyed scan verdict.
#
# SETUP: one Remote PyPI repo over http://mock-pypi/, scan_on_proxy on
# (fail_closed), age gate on (min_age_days 7, mode upstream_publish_time), and
# an `artifacts` row for cuda_toolkit-13.4.2 seeded in the DB so the gate has a
# last-known-good version (the same shape the backend unit test seeds). The
# substitute is the mock's clean wheel.
#
#   (FIX)     GET cuda_toolkit-13.5.0 (young) -> 200 with the 13.4.2 bytes AND
#             `X-AK-Scan: clean`, AND a `clean` proxy_scan_results row for the
#             13.4.2 digest. RED on 1.11.9 (header absent, no verdict row).
#   (CONTROL) both images: the substitute bytes are the mock's 13.4.2 wheel; a
#             direct GET of cuda_toolkit-13.0.3.0 (old, no seeded row) serves
#             200 `X-AK-Scan: clean`; the backend read /pypi/cuda-toolkit/json
#             from the mock.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin login + repo/scan/gate setup + a few GETs.
